// ===================== 8.6 =====================
out.push(h2('8.6  The review, to the shape'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open, timed, and **nobody manages it the first time.** ⚠ Say so before they start, because the point of the stage is not success: it is that the four moves are the whole of the examination task and that forty seconds is enough for all four once the introduction has gone. Run it twice. **The second attempt at thirty seconds beats the first at forty in almost every pair**, and the reason is always the same — the scene-setting goes.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** the **weakness** is missing _(and the ending is a courtesy)_.   **2** the **verdict with its reader** is missing — it begins at the weakness.   **3** the **weakness** is missing again, and this is the commonest shape of all: reader, detail, last line, and nothing wrong with the thing.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — the four moves **are the task**: the examiner marks content, communicative achievement, organisation and language, and the moves answer the first three; and Dima says 180 to 220 words is about four sentences a move, **with no room for an introduction.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** There is **no room for one and no reason for one** — _in this review I am going to look at…_ is twelve words telling the examiner you have read instructions the examiner wrote.   **2** Whether there is **a person in it**, and she is right about it nine times in ten.'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the cycle that converts the unit into marks, and the arithmetic is worth putting on the board: four moves × four sentences = 180–220 words.** Nothing else fits, which is why the introduction has to go — and the introduction is what students write first under time. **Dima\'s advice in the recording is the single most useful thing for a timed task: write the verdict first, even if you intend to cross it out, because you will not cross it out and the rest of the page follows from it.** ⚠ And keep the last minute back: four minutes for the four moves in note form, thirty to write, **one minute at the end to read the last line and ask what the reader does on Monday.** That minute is 8.5 and it is the one candidates give away.'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**1** _(a book)_ _For anybody who reads standing up, this is the one — the print is large enough to read at arm\'s length. What decided it was the glossary at the front. The binding failed in a month. Open it at the glossary and time yourself finding a word._',
  '**2** _(a place to eat)_ _For anybody with twenty minutes, this is the place; for anybody with an hour, it is a waste of an hour. What decided it was that the food is on the counter and not cooked to order. It is noisy enough that you cannot talk. Go once at half past twelve and see whether you are out in twenty minutes._',
  '**3** _(a course)_ _For anybody who has to write at work, this course is the one; for anybody who wants to talk more, it is the wrong course. What decided it was that every cycle ends in a page I actually had to send. There is almost no vocabulary teaching in it. Ask to see one unit\'s Stage 7 before you enrol._',
  '**4** _(a tool)_ _For a busy counter, this set; under five handsets a week, the cheap one. What decided it was that the bits do not round off. The case will not go in a drawer. Count last week\'s handsets before you buy._',
  '**5** _(something you were disappointed by)_ _For anybody who wanted a reference, this is not it; for anybody who wanted a list, it is adequate. What decided it against was that there are no example sentences in about a third of the entries. It is well printed. Look up three words you half know and see whether you are any surer._',
]));
out.push(A('⚠ Mark these on **time and shape, not on content**: four sentences, four moves, no introduction, and the last line doing a different job from the verdict. Item **2** is the one to read out, because its _not for_ reader is so sharply drawn — _for anybody with an hour, it is a waste of an hour_ — and because the test at the end has a figure and a time of day in it. Item **5** is the disappointed case, and note that the four moves work unchanged when the verdict is negative: **the weakness move becomes _what is good about it_**, which is the two-sided review from the other side.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
